    start_*.command         launchers

Fixes applied to the upstream code, with the reasoning recorded in the
comments at each site:

    gui.py    warmup() before the audio stream starts - lazy initialisation on
              the CoreAudio realtime thread overflows its ~512KB stack and
              kills the process with SIGBUS
    gui.py    clamp to +/-1 before inference - resampler overshoot makes
              torchfcpe print from inside the realtime callback
    gui.py    stop_stream() is now unconditional and idempotent, and
              update_devices() calls it before re-initialising PortAudio -
              otherwise IOProcs leak and coreaudiod spins forever

Known problem inherited from upstream, NOT fixed here:

    rvc/f0/models.py and rvc/f0/rmvpe.py both build RMVPE as a five-layer
    placeholder CNN instead of the real U-Net+GRU the checkpoint contains, so
    the rmvpe pitch estimator always fails to load. Use fcpe.
